From ce1b4f03094bfd76de38625b5e28aee5ebb39202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Lemar Gonzales <johnlemargonzales@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:36:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Sync chat history across phones

Adds two personal sync entity types, chat_session and chat_message, so a
student's conversations follow their account to another phone or a
reinstall. They are declared through the existing entity-type negotiation,
so clients that do not declare them never receive them.

- Strict payloads: message text up to 100,000 characters; attachments are
  described (name, format, type, size) but their file location is refused;
  device-only memory notices are refused.
- Last-write-wins edits (the app sends no baseVersion for chat).
- Deleting a chat deletes its messages first; a delete clears the stored
  text and removes the change feed's older copies of it.
- An edit that reaches an already-deleted chat row is a no-op; a new
  message into a deleted or unknown chat recreates that chat untitled.
- POST /v1/sync/chat/purge deletes the account's synchronized chat history
  and nothing else.
- Migration 014 creates both tables with the owner RLS policy.
